# Read by the `ignore` crate (and by ripgrep/fd), NOT by git — which is exactly the point.
#
# Conformance fixture corpora (RFC 0002 §8) are deliberately-flawed test data: checked into
# git and exercised by the conformance harness's own `cargo test` run, but excluded from
# kndo's self-check of its own repo (ROADMAP M1 exit: "kndo check on kndo's own JS-free repo
# returns cleanly"). Analyzing them would report every flaw they were written to contain.
#
# This lived in .gitignore until it silently skipped a newly added fixture — green locally,
# absent from CI, because .gitignore governs `git add` for untracked files. `.ignore` carries
# the same globs to every consumer that needs them and none of the version-control side
# effect, so the exclusion is stated once and means only what it says.
**/tests/fixtures/
